messages:
rina: opened PR to clarify parser behavior around tool_call envelopes vs direct payloads. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/1478. TL;DR: make canonical example show both forms, add note about parsers accepting either.
owen: nice. can we also show a minimal failing example that trips the canonicalizer? helps readers debug. e.g. `{"tool_call": {"name":"run_search", "arguments": "[1,2]"}}` vs `{"query_ids": [1,2]}`
li: good call. also, snippet extractor still prefers fenced triple backticks with a language tag. last time python blocks lost trailing commas; i'll add a regression test in snippets repo.
sam: small nit: avoid ambiguous union shorthand like `string|object` in examples. use explicit `oneOf` and concrete examples so linters and schema viewers behave.
owen: i'll add a canonicalizer unit that asserts envelope + raw both normalize to the same internal shape. also including a short transform example showing snake_case <-> camelCase normalization.
rina: sample ts snippet i'll add: ```ts
// ts (camelCase)
const resp = await client.call({
  model: 'redwood-small',
  input: prompt,
  functions: [{
    name: 'logEvent',
    parameters: {
      type: 'object',
      properties: { eventId: { type: 'string' }, userEmail: { type: 'string' } },
      required: ['eventId']
    }
  }],
  responseMode: 'structured'
})
// parser receives: { eventId: 'evt_123', userEmail: 'u@example.com' }
```
li: LGTM. can we also add a one-line migration note in /docs/migration/function-calling.md calling out removal of ambiguous union examples and linking the new envelope vs raw subsection?
docs-bot: Deploy preview published for PR #1478: https://deploy-preview-1478--redwood-docs.netlify.app/docs/invoke/parser-guidance.html (preview expires in 7 days)
rina: merging after li's snippet tests pass. thanks y'all :tada:
